Object.assign(UI_TRANSLATIONS,{
  "通常的语序是“主语—宾语—动词”。下例中，“我”是主语，“土”是宾语，“挖”放在宾语之后。": "The usual word order is subject–object–verb. In the example below, ‘I’ is the subject, ‘soil’ is the object, and ‘dig’ follows the object.",
  "词类与形容词作谓语": "Word classes and adjectives as predicates",
  "名词用来指人和事物，动词表示动作或状态，代词可以代替名词或名词短语。助词补充“谁的”“正在”“已经”等意义。土家语中许多相当于汉语形容词的词可以直接作谓语，如下面的“今天冷”“他的衣服脏”。": "Nouns refer to people and things, verbs express actions or states, and pronouns can stand for nouns or noun phrases. Particles add meanings such as possession, ongoing action or completion. Many Tujia words corresponding to adjectives can serve directly as predicates, as in ‘Today is cold’ and ‘His clothes are dirty’ below.",
  "结构：主语＋名词（肯定句可以不用“是”）": "Pattern: subject + noun (an affirmative sentence can omit ‘be’)",
  "表示“某处有某人或某物”时，可以先说地点，再说人或物，最后说“有”。下例按“房屋里面＋人＋有”排列。": "To say that someone or something is in a place, the place can come first, followed by the person or thing, then ‘exist’. The example below has the order ‘inside the house + people + exist’.",
  "“这里”“那里”与距离": "‘Here’, ‘there’ and distance",
  "从上下文能知道所说的是什么时，可以省去名词。例如，“小的”可以单独表示“小的那个东西”。": "When the context makes clear what is being discussed, the noun can be left out. For example, ‘the small one’ can refer to a small thing without naming it.",
  "以下例句的顺序：谁的 → 这／那 → 名词 → 描述性质的词 → 数量 → 位置 → 关系词": "Order in the examples below: whose → this/that → noun → property word → quantity → location → relation word",
  "带宾语和不带宾语的句子": "Sentences with and without objects",
  "有宾语时，一般按“主语—宾语—动词”排列，如“姐姐＋弟弟＋打”。没有宾语时，谓语可以直接接在主语后，如“今天＋冷”。": "With an object, the usual order is subject–object–verb, as in ‘elder sister + younger brother + hit’. Without an object, the predicate can follow the subject directly, as in ‘today + cold’.",
  "收到东西或得到帮助的人后面可以加bor，放在表示物品的宾语前。bor也能说明是“对谁说”：下面第一句只用“他”，表示谈论他；第二句在“他”后加bor，表示对他说话。": "bor can follow the person who receives something or benefits from an action, before the object naming the thing involved. It can also show who is being spoken to: the first sentence below uses ‘him’ alone and means talking about him; the second adds bor after ‘him’ and means talking to him.",
  "地点与方位": "Places and positions",
  "表示位置的词放在名词后。例如，“屋里”按“屋＋里面”排列，再加上“人＋有”，组成“屋里有人”。": "Location words follow the noun. For example, ‘inside the house’ has the order ‘house + inside’; adding ‘people + exist’ gives ‘There are people inside the house’.",
  "从哪里来、向哪里去": "Where from and where to",
  "/lie⁵⁵/ 表示“从”，/pɔ⁵⁵/ 表示“向”，都放在表示地点的词语后。": "/lie⁵⁵/ means ‘from’ and /pɔ⁵⁵/ means ‘towards’; both follow the expression naming the place.",
  "徐世璇根据他砂话的田野材料，研究表示地点和方位的词、名词后说明位置的成分，以及物体之间的位置关系。": "Drawing on fieldwork in Tasha, Xu Shixuan studies words for places and directions, elements that follow nouns to indicate location, and spatial relations between objects.",
  "词形变化与动词后的成分": "Word-form changes and elements after verbs",
  "动词和形容词的变化总表": "Overview of verb and adjective forms",
  "作谓语、修饰名词与单独使用": "As predicates, as modifiers and on their own",
  "“好、长、大”等词作谓语时用基本形式，修饰名词时可用另一种词形。后一种形式也能单独表示“好的那个”“长的那个”。": "Words such as ‘good’, ‘long’ and ‘big’ use their basic forms as predicates, but may take a different form when modifying a noun. That form can also stand alone to mean ‘the good one’ or ‘the long one’.",
  "结构：名词＋描述性质的词＋数词和量词": "Pattern: noun + property word + numeral and classifier",
  "比谁更……、相差多少": "Who or what is compared, and by how much",
  "比较时，可以先说拿谁来比较，再说另一个人在哪方面更突出、相差多少。下例先说“我”，再说“他一点胖”，末尾加比较成分，意思是“他比我胖一点”。": "A comparison can begin with the person used for comparison, followed by how the other person differs and by how much. The example starts with ‘me’, then ‘he a little fat’, and ends with a comparison marker: ‘He is a little fatter than me’.",
  "结构：拿来比较的人或物＋另一个人或物＋（相差多少）＋描述性质的词＋niex": "Pattern: person or thing used for comparison + the other person or thing + (amount of difference) + property word + niex",
  "时间与动作的阶段": "Time and stages of an action",
  "“昨天”“明天”等时间词说明动作发生在什么时候。动词的变化和后面的助词，还可以表达“正在做”“做完了”“做过”等区别。": "Time words such as ‘yesterday’ and ‘tomorrow’ say when an action takes place. Changes in the verb and particles after it can also show whether an action is ongoing, finished or part of a past experience.",
  "术语和例句缩写对照": "Terms and abbreviations used in examples",
  "用 /i/ 表示计划和预期": "Using /i/ for plans and expectations",
  "要做、快要做与开始做": "Planning, being about to act and starting",
  "正在做、做着与还在做": "Doing, remaining in a state and still doing",
  "做了与做完了": "Doing something and finishing it",
  "过去的经历与现在的结果": "Past experience and present results",
  "位置与动作的方向": "Location and the direction of an action",
  "名词后的“里面”“外面”等词说明位置；动词后的成分可以表示“向这里来”“向别处去”，说明动作的方向。": "Words such as ‘inside’ and ‘outside’ follow nouns to describe location; elements after verbs can mean ‘towards here’ or ‘away from here’, describing the direction of an action.",
  "“是”与“有”": "‘Be’ and ‘exist’",
  "有些句子直接用名词作谓语，有些会加上相当于“是”的词。/sou²⁴/ 常用来作肯定回答，也可放在作谓语的名词后。": "Some sentences use a noun directly as the predicate; others add a word meaning ‘be’. /sou²⁴/ often serves as an affirmative answer and can also follow a noun used as the predicate.",
  "“使、让”句": "Sentences with ‘make’ or ‘let’",
  "用dor表示“使、让”": "Using dor for ‘make’ or ‘let’",
  "表示“让谁做什么”时，dor放在这个人后面、动作前面。它可以表示使某人做，也可以表示允许某人做。有时句子强调某人受到动作的影响，译成汉语时会带有“被”的意味。": "To say ‘make or let someone do something’, dor comes after the person and before the action. It can mean causing someone to act or allowing them to act. In some contexts, the sentence emphasizes how someone is affected by an action and can have a passive sense.",
  "结构：谁让＋让谁＋dor＋做什么": "Pattern: person making or letting + person acting + dor + action",
  "动词后各成分的顺序": "Order of elements after the verb",
  "也能表示这里用ci表达的“吃的东西”等意思。不同说话人、不同句子中，xi和ci怎样选择，仍需结合具体例句比较。": "can express meanings such as ‘something to eat’, for which ci is used here. The choice between xi and ci still needs to be compared across particular speakers and sentences.",
  "“做的人”“吃的人”“看的人”都可以单独指某一类人，也可以作主语，后接“人少”一类谓语。": "‘People who do’, ‘people who eat’ and ‘people who look’ can stand alone to refer to those people, or serve as subjects followed by a predicate such as ‘are few’.",
  "下面两句都表示“我要吃金花不能吃的东西”，区别在“东西”的位置：第一句放在从句之后，第二句放在从句里面、动词“吃”之前。方括号划出从句范围。": "Both sentences below mean ‘I want to eat what Jinhua cannot eat’. They differ in the position of ‘thing’: it follows the clause in the first sentence and stays inside the clause, before ‘eat’, in the second. Square brackets mark the clause boundaries.",
  "我要吃金花不能吃的东西。（名词在从句外）": "I will eat what Jinhua cannot eat. (Noun outside the clause)",
  "我要吃金花不能吃的东西。（名词在从句内）": "I will eat what Jinhua cannot eat. (Noun inside the clause)",
  "补充：名词留在从句内时有哪些限制": "More: restrictions when the noun stays inside the clause",
  "带宾语的动词：怎样指做事的人": "Verbs with objects: referring to the person acting",
  "在Liu的材料中，名词留在从句里时，可以用来指宾语，或不带宾语的动词的主语。下面“孩子吃食物”中的“吃”带有宾语“食物”；要指“孩子”时，把“孩子”放在从句外的说法成立，留在从句内的说法不成立。星号表示原文判为不合语法。": "In Liu’s data, a noun kept inside the clause can refer to its object, or to the subject of a verb without an object. In ‘the child eats food’ below, ‘eat’ has the object ‘food’. To refer to the child, the version with ‘child’ outside the clause is accepted; the version with it inside is not. An asterisk marks a form judged ungrammatical in the source.",
  "想表达同一意思，但把“孩子”留在从句内，原文判为不合语法。": "Intended to express the same meaning, but with ‘child’ inside the clause; the source judges it ungrammatical.",
  "下面两句对 /la²¹/ 的使用也不同：“鸟”放在从句外时，可以加 /la²¹/；“鸟”留在从句内时，就不能加。括号表示可省略，括号里的星号表示加上后不合语法。": "The two sentences below also differ in their use of /la²¹/: it is allowed when ‘bird’ is outside the clause, but not when ‘bird’ stays inside. Parentheses mark an optional element; an asterisk inside them means that adding it makes the sentence ungrammatical.",
  "金花喂了我经常看到的鸟。（名词在从句外）": "Jinhua fed the bird I often see. (Noun outside the clause)",
  "金花喂了我经常看到的鸟。（名词在从句内；不能加 /la²¹/）": "Jinhua fed the bird I often see. (Noun inside the clause; /la²¹/ is not allowed)",
  "从句里再包含一句话": "A clause containing another clause",
  "从句里面再包含一句话时，情况会不同。下面“我记得［孩子打破碗］”里面的“孩子”就可以留在从句内：": "The result can differ when one clause contains another. In ‘I remember [the child broke the bowl]’ below, ‘child’ can stay inside the clause:",
  "Liu将名词留在从句内的形式分析为较小的结构（TP），把名词放在从句外的形式分析为较大的结构（CP），并用名词在句法结构中移动的距离解释这些差异。这是该研究提出的理论分析；单凭这些限制，还不能判断土家语在一般句子中怎样区分主语和宾语。": "Liu analyses the form with the noun inside the clause as a smaller structure (TP), and the form with the noun outside as a larger one (CP), explaining the differences through the distance the noun moves in the syntactic structure. This is the study’s theoretical analysis; these restrictions alone do not establish how Tujia generally distinguishes subjects and objects.",
  "作者认为，这种用法通过表示动作的词来描写静止的状态。": "The authors analyse this use as describing a static situation with words that express movement.",
  "话题、停顿与代词": "Topics, pauses and pronouns",
  "话题是正在谈论的人或事物，不一定是主语。话题常放在句首，后面可以稍作停顿，再用gof指前面提到的人。第一例先提出“弟弟”，再用代词指他；第二例的“姐姐”同时也是后面动作的主语。": "The topic is the person or thing being discussed and need not be the subject. It often comes first, followed by a short pause; gof can then refer to the person already mentioned. The first example introduces ‘younger brother’ and refers to him with a pronoun; in the second, ‘elder sister’ is also the subject of the following action.",
  "后面的句子可以继续谈同一话题，也可以用代词再次提到它。第三人称代词既能指前面的主语，也能指放到句首的宾语。": "Following clauses can continue the same topic or refer to it again with a pronoun. A third-person pronoun can refer either to the earlier subject or to an object placed at the start of the sentence.",
  "南北表达“给”的方式": "Ways of expressing ‘give’ in Northern and Southern Tujia",
  "北部和南部表达“给”时，都可以把收到东西的人放在物品前。下面的龙山例在人称代词后加 /po⁵⁵/，泸溪且己例没有对应的成分。": "When expressing ‘give’, both Northern and Southern Tujia can place the recipient before the thing given. The Longshan example below adds /po⁵⁵/ after the personal pronoun; the Luxi Qieji example has no corresponding element.",
  "下例中，“你”是表示接受者的间接宾语，“铜钱”是直接宾语，两个宾语后均无关系词。": "In the following example, “you” is the indirect object, identifying the recipient, and “money” is the direct object. Neither object is followed by a relational particle.",
  "名词后的关系词": "Relation words after nouns",
  "其他名词后的关系词（待补充）": "Other relation words after nouns (to be added)",
  "前缀声调随词根变化": "Prefix tones change with the root",
  "前缀的实际声调": "Actual prefix tone",
  "名词化让动词、形容词或一句话可以像名词一样使用。例如，“吃”可以组成“吃的东西”，“做工”可以组成“做工的人”，“吃饭”可以组成“吃饭的地方”。北部土家语材料中可见以下四种名词化形式：": "Nominalization allows a verb, adjective or a whole clause to be used like a noun. For example, ‘eat’ can form an expression meaning ‘something to eat’, ‘work’ can form ‘someone who works’, and ‘eat a meal’ can form ‘a place to eat’. Northern Tujia sources record the following four nominalizing forms:",
  "名词化也可以指一件事。例如，“看［哭嫁］”把哭嫁当作观看的对象；“［耕地］好”则评价耕地这件事。xi可以接在动作短语后，也可以接在整个小句后。这里的“小句”指句子中含有谓语的一段话，如“我怕［他跑掉］”中的“他跑掉”。": "Nominalization can also refer to an event. In ‘watch [the bridal lament]’, the lament is what is watched; ‘[ploughing the field] is good’ evaluates the event of ploughing. xi can follow an action phrase or a whole clause. A clause is a unit containing a predicate, such as ‘he runs away’ in ‘I fear [he will run away]’."
});

