Object.assign(UI_TRANSLATIONS,{
  "日语可比形式": "Comparable Japanese forms",
  "が ga（功能部分相近）": "が ga (partly comparable in function)",
  "有主语助词、可选作格和回指代词等分析；不及物句中也有相关记录，分析存在分歧。": "Analyzed as a subject particle, optional ergative or resumptive pronoun; occurrences in intransitive clauses are also documented, with differing analyses.",
  "/te²¹/；亦记/tiɛ⁵⁵/": "/te²¹/; also recorded as /tiɛ⁵⁵/",
  "提示、强调主语或宾语": "Highlighting or emphasizing subjects and objects",
  "は wa（提示）；も mo（“连……都……”）": "は wa (highlighting); も mo (“even”)",
  "《简志》列为主语标志；李启群等词典明确记载其用于主语或宾语后，张伟权词典另见时间成分后的用例。": "A subject marker in the Outline; Li Qiqun et al. explicitly document it after subjects and objects, and Zhang Weiquan also records it after a temporal expression.",
  "无直接对应的格助词": "No directly corresponding case particle",
  "和、跟、同……一起": "And, with, together with",
  "と to（并列、伴随）": "と to (coordination and accompaniment)",
  "张伟权词典列为连词，兼有连接名词和表示共同参与的用法；后者由前者脱落第二个音节而来。": "Listed as conjunctions in Zhang Weiquan’s dictionary, joining nouns or expressing joint participation; the shorter form loses the second syllable of the longer form.",
  "带宾语的句子一般按“主语—宾语—动词”排列，如“姐姐＋弟弟＋打”。没有宾语时，谓语可以直接接在前面的名词性成分后，如“今天＋冷”。": "Clauses with an object normally follow subject–object–verb order, as in “elder sister + younger brother + hit”. Without an object, the predicate can directly follow the preceding nominal expression, as in “today + cold”.",
  "/kuɔ²⁴/：主语标记、作格与回指代词": "/kuɔ²⁴/: subject marking, ergative case and resumptive pronouns",
  "一般主语标记可以同时用于“我打他”和“我来了”两类句子的主语；作格标记的核心用法是标记前一类，即及物句的主语。": "A general subject marker can occur with the subjects of both “I hit him” and “I came”. The core function of an ergative marker is to mark the former type: the subject of a transitive clause.",
  "Liu、Ran与Xiang的合著未刊稿将/kʊo²⁴/（变调时为/kʊo⁴⁴/）分析为可选作格标记，并将这一用法限定于及物主语。他们把相关不及物例句中的同形形式分析为回指代词，例如把“小孩＋该形式＋睡着了”理解为“小孩，他睡着了”。": "The unpublished manuscript by Liu, Ran and Xiang analyzes /kʊo²⁴/ (with tone-sandhi form /kʊo⁴⁴/) as an optional ergative marker, restricting this use to transitive subjects. They analyze homophonous forms in the relevant intransitive examples as resumptive pronouns, reading “child + this form + fell asleep” as “The child, he fell asleep”.",
  "文献中有/ko³⁵/出现在不及物句主语后的记录，其语法身份存在分歧。除《简志》的“小孩睡着了”外，Lu等（2019）的公开数据还有“弟弟大声哭了”及第一人称后接该形式的“住”类例句。后者与Liu等回指代词分析的关系仍有待进一步核实。": "Sources record /ko³⁵/ after intransitive subjects, but its grammatical status is disputed. In addition to “The child fell asleep” in the Outline, the published data of Lu et al. (2019) include “Younger brother cried loudly” and an example with a first-person subject followed by this form and a predicate meaning “stay”. How the latter relates to Liu et al.’s resumptive-pronoun analysis requires further verification.",
  "WALS，第98章：完整名词短语的格标记配列": "WALS, Chapter 98: Alignment of Case Marking of Full Noun Phrases",
  "《土家语简志》（1986），第93页。Lu、van de Weijer、Ma与Liu（2019），": "Outline of Tujia (1986), p. 93. Lu, van de Weijer, Ma and Liu (2019), ",
  "，表1、例20b、30B及66组。第一人称“住”类例句出自哭嫁歌，原文开头为/ŋa³⁵ (ko³⁵)/；其句法和韵律仍需结合原始语料复核。": ", Table 1 and examples 20b, 30B and the group numbered 66. The first-person “stay” example comes from a wedding lament and begins /ŋa³⁵ (ko³⁵)/; its syntax and prosody need to be checked against the original material.",
  "/te²¹/：提示与强调": "/te²¹/: highlighting and emphasis",
  "/te²¹/在李启群等《土家语汉语词典》中记作/tiɛ⁵⁵/。这个助词接在名词性成分后，突出说话人所强调的对象，可以用于主语，也可以用于宾语。": "/te²¹/ is recorded as /tiɛ⁵⁵/ in Li Qiqun et al.’s Tujia–Chinese Dictionary. This particle follows a nominal expression and highlights its referent. It can be used with both subjects and objects.",
  "《土家语简志》将它列为突出、强调主语的结构助词。例如：": "The Outline of Tujia lists it as a structural particle that highlights or emphasizes the subject. For example:",
  "李启群等《土家语汉语词典》对其分布的说明更完整：它用于作主语或宾语的名词性词语后，强调该词语所指的对象，汉译时通常不必译出。下面一句中的/tiɛ⁵⁵/就跟在宾语“奥梯桔的儿子”之后：": "Li Qiqun et al.’s Tujia–Chinese Dictionary gives a fuller description of its distribution: it follows nominal expressions serving as subjects or objects, emphasizing their referents, and usually needs no separate Chinese translation. In the following sentence, /tiɛ⁵⁵/ follows the object “Aotiju’s son”:",
  "出处：李启群等《土家语汉语词典》（2021），/tiɛ⁵⁵/助词条；逐词释义据原句补列。": "Source: Li Qiqun et al., Tujia–Chinese Dictionary (2021), the /tiɛ⁵⁵/ particle entry; word-by-word glosses have been added.",
  "张伟权《土家语汉语词典》（2002）也有/te²¹/跟在宾语和时间表达后的例句（第210、41页）。因此，“主语标志”只概括了它的一部分用法；从这些材料来看，将它描述为提示、强调有关成分的助词，更能涵盖它的分布。": "Zhang Weiquan’s Tujia–Chinese Dictionary (2002) also has examples of /te²¹/ following an object or a temporal expression (pp. 210, 41). “Subject marker” therefore describes only part of its use; a particle highlighting or emphasizing a constituent better captures its distribution in these sources.",
  "，贵阳：贵州民族出版社，第41、210页。": ", Guiyang: Guizhou Nationalities Press, pp. 41, 210.",
  "，北京：商务印书馆，/tiɛ⁵⁵/助词条。该书与张伟权（2002）的同名词典为不同著作。": ", Beijing: The Commercial Press, the /tiɛ⁵⁵/ particle entry. This is a different work from Zhang Weiquan’s 2002 dictionary of the same title.",
  "/ta⁵³xa²¹/、/ta⁵⁵/：和、同……一起": "/ta⁵³xa²¹/, /ta⁵⁵/: and, together with",
  "/ta⁵³xa²¹/和/ta⁵⁵/可以表示“和、跟、同……一起”。张伟权《土家语汉语词典》将两者列为连词，并说明/ta⁵⁵/是/ta⁵³xa²¹/脱落/xa²¹/音节后的形式。这些用法可以与日语と to连接名词、引出共同参与者的功能比较。": "/ta⁵³xa²¹/ and /ta⁵⁵/ can mean “and, with, together with”. Zhang Weiquan’s Tujia–Chinese Dictionary lists both as conjunctions and explains that /ta⁵⁵/ derives from /ta⁵³xa²¹/ by loss of the syllable /xa²¹/. Their functions can be compared with Japanese と to in joining nouns and introducing a co-participant.",
  "，第42、44页；日语と的并列、伴随用法见东京外国语大学": ", pp. 42, 44; for coordination and accompaniment with Japanese to, see the Tokyo University of Foreign Studies module on ",
  "第Ⅹ节。": ", section X.",
  "话题还可以用/lɤ/、/mɤ/标示；宾语话题、时间话题及其与提示、强调助词/te²¹/的区别，见": "Topics can also be marked by /lɤ/ and /mɤ/. For object and temporal topics and their relation to the highlighting and emphatic particle /te²¹/, see "
});

