Object.assign(UI_TRANSLATIONS, {
  "英语里，Reading is fun（读书很有趣）用动名词 reading 作主语，I like reading（我喜欢读书）用它作宾语。这两句都把“读书”这个动作当作一件事来谈。宾语也可以是一整个从句：I know that he likes books（我知道他喜欢书）中，that he likes books 是 know 的宾语，说明“知道”的内容。": "In Reading is fun, the gerund reading is the subject; in I like reading, it is the object. Both sentences treat reading as an activity to talk about. An object can also be a whole clause: in I know that he likes books, that he likes books is the object of know and expresses what is known.",
  "土家语也能把动作或小句作为主语、宾语，常用的形式是在动作短语或小句后加 xi。这里的“小句”指含有谓语的一段话，例如“我怕［他跑掉］”中的“他跑掉”。": "Tujia can likewise use actions or clauses as subjects and objects, commonly by adding xi after the action phrase or clause. A clause is a unit containing a predicate, such as ‘he runs away’ in ‘I fear [he will run away]’.",
  "英语里的 the book that I like（我喜欢的书）包含一个定语从句：that I like 修饰 book，说明是哪一本书。定语从句也叫关系从句；book 在中学英语语法里叫先行词，从整个名词短语的结构看，它是中心名词。": "In the book that I like, the relative clause that I like modifies book, identifying which book is meant. In school grammar, book is called the antecedent; within the noun phrase, it is the head noun.",
  "英语把这个从句放在名词后，汉语“我喜欢的书”则把“我喜欢的”放在“书”前。土家语的关系从句也放在中心名词前，修饰语与名词之间常见 nie、xi 或 nie-xi。": "English places this clause after the noun; Chinese puts the equivalent of ‘that I like’ before ‘book’. Tujia relative clauses also precede the head noun, with nie, xi or nie-xi commonly occurring between the modifier and the noun."
});

